Analysis

A critical section prevents multiple threads from modifying the shared accumulation variable simultaneously. This eliminates the race condition and produces a correct numerical result.

However, synchronization introduces additional overhead. Threads must wait when another thread is inside the critical section. Therefore, although the computation is parallelized, access to the shared accumulator becomes a serialized part of the program.

