6. Task 2.4 — Speedup and Efficiency

Objective

The objective is to calculate the speedup and parallel efficiency using the average execution times from Task 2.3.

Speedup is calculated as:

[
S(P)=\frac{T(1)}{T(P)}
]

Parallel efficiency is calculated as:

[
E(P)=\frac{S(P)}{P}
]

The ideal linear speedup is equal to the number of threads:

[
S_{ideal}(P)=P
]

